    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d886">

                <pb facs="0977" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/685: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-19T18:00:00-04:00">September 19,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Your 176, September 16, 3 p.m. Department has no objection to President
                        Moncada’s suggestion that the
                    candidates should sign an agreement in your presence that they will carry out
                    the provisions <pb facs="0978" n="874" xml:id="pg874"/> of the plan proposed by
                    the Commander of the Guardia and accepted by President Moncada, for the appointment of the higher
                    officers in the Guardia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
